Nice!

563
00:29:45,270 --> 00:29:46,270
Something's off.

564
00:29:46,400 --> 00:29:49,200
I've never seen Zhou Xiangxiang
act this awkward before.

565
00:29:49,200 --> 00:29:51,310
There's definitely something
going on between those two.

566
00:29:51,310 --> 00:29:52,480
I think so, too.

567
00:29:52,830 --> 00:29:54,920
If they could see each other more often,

568
00:29:54,920 --> 00:29:56,650
maybe they could break the ice.

569
00:29:57,240 --> 00:29:59,900
But given how things are
between them right now,

570
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:02,270
I doubt either of them
wants to see the other.

571
00:30:02,270 --> 00:30:03,600
Why don't we just come up

572
00:30:04,200 --> 00:30:05,260
with a good excuse?

573
00:30:06,830 --> 00:30:08,030
Like what?

574
00:30:09,070 --> 00:30:10,000
[Rental Agreement]

575
00:30:11,030 --> 00:30:12,290
A housewarming party?

576
00:30:13,310 --> 00:30:14,240
That could work.

577
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:16,750
Rhyme

578
00:30:16,790 --> 00:30:19,650
is one of the fundamental elements
of poetic meter.

579
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:22,110
When a poet uses rhyme in a poem,

580
00:30:22,110 --> 00:30:23,880
we call it rhyming.

581
00:30:23,960 --> 00:30:26,720
From "The Book of Songs" to modern poetry,

582
00:30:24,690 --> 00:30:26,650
[Rhyming]

583
00:30:26,750 --> 00:30:28,400
almost all poems rhyme.

584
00:30:28,790 --> 00:30:30,480
In northern Chinese opera,

585
00:30:30,550 --> 00:30:32,680
rhyme is also called "zhe,"

586
00:30:32,680 --> 00:30:35,000
and rhyming is known as "he zhe."

587
